# Phase 075 — Teach the language server navigation: goto-definition, references, completion

## What changed

| File | Lines | What |
|---|---|---|
| src/lsp.rs | +1005 −1 | `Location`, `Definition`, `DefinitionKind`; token-level lexical scope walk; `goto_definition`, `find_references`, `completions` and their JSON forms; greedy string-literal and `//` comment context checks; balanced `else if`, multi-name `set`, typed/`of` parameters, catch binders, object-only `has`, range `to` recognition, decorator-position checks, and function-literal frames for keyword-started bodies |
| src/lib.rs | +3 −2 | re-export the new navigation surface |
| tests/tooling_grammar_test.rs | +663 −2 | 26 navigation tests (23 `edge_*`) including shadowing, builtins, imports, Unicode, comments, malformed source and positions, nested loop/object scopes, `else if`, multi-assignment, typed parameters, catch binders, membership `has`, range bounds, function literals and the 5000-line benchmark |
| tests/unreviewed_work_ack_test.rs | +1 −0 | add `resume phase-075:` to the delivery-subject rule so this phase's rebuildable delivery commit is acknowledged by subject, not by a stale SHA |

No server loop or transport was added: the phase asks for pure functions over source text, and the existing `diagnostics_json` shape is extended per capability.

