Fixed all four findings:

- `set`/`constant` now reuse an enclosing binding (write-through) instead of shadowing it.
- One-line function literals close at the parsed body's delimiter, so same-line trailing arguments resolve outside the literal.
- `inside_comment` treats the terminating newline/EOF boundary as inside the comment.
- The benchmark now asserts linear scaling (1000 vs 5000 lines) instead of a wall-clock threshold.

Added 3 boundary/navigation tests and updated `REPORT.md`. All four gates pass: `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy -D warnings`, `cargo test --all-targets` (2779 passed), and `../rbops/verify.sh "phase-075"`.
